texts.NKJV:
Vindicate me, O God,
And plead my cause against an ungodly nation;
Oh, deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man!

For You are the God of my strength;
Why do You cast me off?
Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?

texts.NASB95:
O send out Your light and Your truth, let them lead me;
Let them bring me to Your holy hill
And to Your dwelling places.

texts.ESV:
Send out your light and your truth;
    let them lead me;
let them bring me to your holy hill
    and to your dwelling!

texts.NASB95:
Then I will go to the altar of God,
To God my exceeding joy;
And upon the lyre I shall praise You, O God, my God.

Then You will delight in righteous sacrifices,
In burnt offering and whole burnt offering;
Then young bulls will be offered on Your altar.

texts.NKJV:
Then You shall be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness,
With burnt offering and whole burnt offering;
Then they shall offer bulls on Your altar.

texts.ESV:
then will you delight in right sacrifices,
    in burnt offerings and whole burnt offerings;
    then bulls will be offered on your altar.

texts.NASB95:
For strangers have risen against me
And violent men have sought my life;
They have not set God before them. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
For strangers have risen up against me,
And oppressors have sought after my life;
They have not set God before them. Selah

texts.ESV:
For strangers have risen against me;
    ruthless men seek my life;
    they do not set God before themselves. Selah

Day and night they go around it
    on its walls,
and iniquity and trouble are within it;

ruin is in its midst;
oppression and fraud
    do not depart from its marketplace.

texts.NKJV:
For it is not an enemy who reproaches me;
Then I could bear it.
Nor is it one who hates me who has exalted himself against me;
Then I could hide from him.

texts.NASB95:
Let death come deceitfully upon them;
Let them go down alive to Sheol,
For evil is in their dwelling, in their midst.

texts.NKJV:
Let death seize them;
Let them go down alive into hell,
For wickedness is in their dwellings and among them.

texts.ESV:
Let death steal over them;
    let them go down to Sheol alive;
    for evil is in their dwelling place and in their heart.

He redeems my soul in safety
    from the battle that I wage,
    for many are arrayed against me.

texts.NKJV:
Cast your burden on the Lord,
And He shall sustain you;
He shall never permit the righteous to be moved.

texts.NASB95:
But You, O God, will bring them down to the pit of destruction;
Men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days.
But I will trust in You.

texts.NKJV:
But You, O God, shall bring them down to the pit of destruction;
Bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days;
But I will trust in You.

texts.ESV:
They stir up strife, they lurk;
    they watch my steps,
    as they have waited for my life.

texts.NASB95:
You have taken account of my wanderings;
Put my tears in Your bottle.
Are they not in Your book?

texts.NKJV:
You number my wanderings;
Put my tears into Your bottle;
Are they not in Your book?

texts.ESV:
You have kept count of my tossings;
    put my tears in your bottle.
    Are they not in your book?

texts.NKJV:
When I cry out to You,
Then my enemies will turn back;
This I know, because God is for me.

In God I have put my trust;
I will not be afraid.
What can man do to me?

texts.NASB95:
He will send from heaven and save me;
He reproaches him who tramples upon me. Selah.
God will send forth His lovingkindness and His truth.

texts.NKJV:
He shall send from heaven and save me;
He reproaches the one who would swallow me up. Selah
God shall send forth His mercy and His truth.

texts.ESV:
He will send from heaven and save me;
    he will put to shame him who tramples on me. Selah
God will send out his steadfast love and his faithfulness!

texts.NASB95:
They have prepared a net for my steps;
My soul is bowed down;
They dug a pit before me;
They themselves have fallen into the midst of it. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
They have prepared a net for my steps;
My soul is bowed down;
They have dug a pit before me;
Into the midst of it they themselves have fallen. Selah

O God, You have cast us off;
You have broken us down;
You have been displeased;
Oh, restore us again!

You have made the earth tremble;
You have broken it;
Heal its breaches, for it is shaking.

texts.NASB95:
“Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim also is the helmet of My head;
Judah is My scepter.

texts.NKJV:
Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim also is the helmet for My head;
Judah is My lawgiver.

texts.ESV:
Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine;
    Ephraim is my helmet;
    Judah is my scepter.

texts.NASB95:
“Moab is My washbowl;
Over Edom I shall throw My shoe;
Shout loud, O Philistia, because of Me!”

texts.NKJV:
Moab is My washpot;
Over Edom I will cast My shoe;
Philistia, shout in triumph because of Me.”

texts.ESV:
Moab is my washbasin;
    upon Edom I cast my shoe;
    over Philistia I shout in triumph.”

texts.NKJV:
From the end of the earth I will cry to You,
When my heart is overwhelmed;
Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.

Iniquities prevail against me;
As for our transgressions,
You will provide atonement for them.

texts.NASB95:
You visit the earth and cause it to overflow;
You greatly enrich it;
The stream of God is full of water;
You prepare their grain, for thus You prepare the earth.

texts.NKJV:
You visit the earth and water it,
You greatly enrich it;
The river of God is full of water;
You provide their grain,
For so You have prepared it.

texts.ESV:
You visit the earth and water it;
    you greatly enrich it;
the river of God is full of water;
    you provide their grain,
    for so you have prepared it.

texts.NASB95:
The meadows are clothed with flocks
And the valleys are covered with grain;
They shout for joy, yes, they sing.

texts.NKJV:
The pastures are clothed with flocks;
The valleys also are covered with grain;
They shout for joy, they also sing.

texts.NASB95:
“All the earth will worship You,
And will sing praises to You;
They will sing praises to Your name.” Selah.

texts.NKJV:
All the earth shall worship You
And sing praises to You;
They shall sing praises to Your name.” Selah

texts.ESV:
All the earth worships you
    and sings praises to you;
    they sing praises to your name.” Selah

texts.NASB95:
He turned the sea into dry land;
They passed through the river on foot;
There let us rejoice in Him!

texts.NKJV:
He turned the sea into dry land;
They went through the river on foot.
There we will rejoice in Him.

texts.ESV:
He turned the sea into dry land;
    they passed through the river on foot.
There did we rejoice in him,

texts.NASB95:
He rules by His might forever;
His eyes keep watch on the nations;
Let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
He rules by His power forever;
His eyes observe the nations;
Do not let the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah

texts.NASB95:
You made men ride over our heads;
We went through fire and through water,
Yet You brought us out into a place of abundance.

texts.NKJV:
You have caused men to ride over our heads;
We went through fire and through water;
But You brought us out to rich fulfillment.

texts.ESV:
you let men ride over our heads;
    we went through fire and through water;
yet you have brought us out to a place of abundance.

texts.NASB95:
I shall offer to You burnt offerings of fat beasts,
With the smoke of rams;
I shall make an offering of bulls with male goats. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
I will offer You burnt sacrifices of fat animals,
With the sweet aroma of rams;
I will offer bulls with goats. Selah

texts.ESV:
I will offer to you burnt offerings of fattened animals,
    with the smoke of the sacrifice of rams;
I will make an offering of bulls and goats. Selah

texts.NKJV:
I am weary with my crying;
My throat is dry;
My eyes fail while I wait for my God.

texts.NASB95:
Those who hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of my head;
Those who would destroy me are powerful, being wrongfully my enemies;
What I did not steal, I then have to restore.

texts.NKJV:
Those who hate me without a cause
Are more than the hairs of my head;
They are mighty who would destroy me,
Being my enemies wrongfully;
Though I have stolen nothing,
I still must restore it.

texts.ESV:
Let not those who hope in you be put to shame through me,
    O Lord God of hosts;
let not those who seek you be brought to dishonor through me,
    O God of Israel.

texts.NASB95:
But as for me, my prayer is to You, O Lord, at an acceptable time;
O God, in the greatness of Your lovingkindness,
Answer me with Your saving truth.

texts.NKJV:
Let not the floodwater overflow me,
Nor let the deep swallow me up;
And let not the pit shut its mouth on me.

And do not hide Your face from Your servant,
For I am in trouble;
Hear me speedily.

texts.ESV:
You know my reproach,
    and my shame and my dishonor;
    my foes are all known to you.

texts.NKJV:
Reproach has broken my heart,
And I am full of heaviness;
I looked for someone to take pity, but there was none;
And for comforters, but I found none.

texts.ESV:
For God will save Zion
    and build up the cities of Judah,
and people shall dwell there and possess it;

texts.NASB95:
Let all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You;
And let those who love Your salvation say continually,
“Let God be magnified.”

texts.NKJV:
Let all those who seek You rejoice and be glad in You;
And let those who love Your salvation say continually,
“Let God be magnified!”

texts.NASB95:
But I am afflicted and needy;
Hasten to me, O God!
You are my help and my deliverer;
O Lord, do not delay.

texts.NKJV:
But I am poor and needy;
Make haste to me, O God!
You are my help and my deliverer;
O Lord, do not delay.

texts.ESV:
But I am poor and needy;
    hasten to me, O God!
You are my help and my deliverer;
    O Lord, do not delay!
